      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village sits in a natural gap cut through the treeline, a feature that shaped its early settlement patterns.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bone_Gap%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early families such as the Rudes, Morgans, Knowltons, Phillipses, Leachs, Gibsons, Rices, and Goulds helped establish the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bone_Gap%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Before the current village, Old Bone Gap—known as Yankeetown—hosted a store, post office, doctor’s office, blacksmith, Baptist church, and Methodist parsonage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bone_Gap%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Bone Gap lies just 7 miles northeast of Albion, the Edwards County seat, placing it in the county’s northeastern quadrant.",
